UPDATE companies SET description='H&H Metals was founded in 1991 in Thornton, Colorado, as a custom sheet metal fabrication job shop serving the Denver metropolitan area. The company operates from a facility on Grant Drive and focuses on architectural sheet metal work, including the manufacture of aluminum sunshades and light shelves.

The shop provides laser cutting, bending and forming, shearing and blanking, CNC routing, and welding, supported by a large in-stock inventory of steel, stainless steel, and aluminum sheet, plate, tubing, flat bar, and angle. An internal order tracking system called O.T.I.S. gives customers real-time email updates on project status, and the company offers design services for sunshade clips along with detailed installation drawings, though it does not perform installation itself.

H&H Metals serves the architectural and commercial construction markets, supplying products such as architectural aluminum sunshades, sun control devices, BrightShelf® lightshelves, ornamental and decorative metals, aluminum composite material (ACM) panels, metal wall panels, and insulated spandrel infill panels.

