UPDATE companies SET description='Harpak-ULMA Packaging, LLC is headquartered in Taunton, Massachusetts. The business traces its roots to 1994 when the Harlfinger family, drawing on over 30 years of packaging experience, established Harpak. On July 19, 2010, Harpak merged with ULMA Packaging—a company with more than 50 years of equipment and systems expertise—to form the current entity. The combined organization maintains a family-business atmosphere and emphasizes long-term customer relationships.

The company supplies end-to-end weighing, distribution, and packaging solutions, including vertical form-fill-seal (VFFS) machines, tray sealers, thermoformers, vision inspection systems, and metal detection/rejection equipment. It also provides installation, factory acceptance testing (including remote FAT), operator and maintenance training through its AICET-accredited academy, preventive maintenance programs, and a 24/7/365 parts and technical support network staffed by PMMI-certified technicians. Harpak-ULMA operates across North America with a field service presence and holds an NPS of 84 percent.

Primary markets include food processing (bakery, poultry, cheese, snack, and case-ready packaging), medical device packaging, and industrial packaging. The firm works with corporations in those sectors and, since 2024, supports Cabinplant weighing and packaging equipment owners in the U.S. and Canada through a full partnership.

Harpak-ULMA cites its six core values—integrity, commitment, service, excellence, teamwork, and innovation—as the foundation of its differentiation. The merger combined ULMA’s advanced design and manufacturing technologies with Harpak’s cultivated customer relationships, aiming to deliver a wider range of fully integrated packaging solutions while preserving a personal, family-business approach.', certifications=ARRAY['PMMI certified technicians','AICET accredited (Harpak-ULMA Packaging Academy)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Weighing solutions", "Distribution solutions", "Vertical form-fill-seal (VFFS) packaging", "Tray sealing", "Thermoforming", "Vision inspection (tray sealed, thermoformed, skin pack)", "Metal detection and rejection", "Preventive maintenance", "Installation and setup (including FAT, remote FAT)", "Operator training", "Maintenance training", "Remote training and troubleshooting", "Harpak-ULMA Packaging Academy (CEUs)", "Parts supply and inventory management", "Technical phone support", "On-site field service", "Packaging line integration", "Sustainable packaging consulting", "Robotic loading systems", "Washdown VFFS (IP66)", "Case-ready packaging", "Bar code inspection", "Print inspection", "Film inspection"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Medical device packaging", "Industrial packaging", "Bakery production", "Poultry production", "Cheese packaging", "Snack packaging", "Case-ready packaging", "Weighing and packaging solutions (Cabinplant)"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["VTC 840 WD (Full IP66 Washdown VFFS)", "Hygienic Robotic Loading Platform with Integrated Rockwell Automation Controls", "ULMA Vision vision inspection systems", "Metal detector/rejection systems (push-arm type)", "Tray sealing equipment", "Thermoforming equipment", "Stand-alone skin pack inspection unit"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7/365 dedicated support and maintenance", "NPS of 84% (nearly triple the packaging OEM average