UPDATE companies SET description='Hawaii Medical Research Center operates a cadaver laboratory in Honolulu, Hawaii, established to provide a dedicated venue for medical education, research, and surgical skill development. The facility was created in response to growing societal concern for medical safety and rapid advances in medical technology, which have increased demand for hands-on training that cannot be conducted on living patients.

The center provides a fully equipped cadaver lab where physicians, dentists, and other healthcare professionals can practice advanced surgical techniques, test new medical devices, and conduct anatomical research. Cadavers are sourced through the American Association of Tissue Banks, with each donor screened for infectious disease and accompanied by safety documentation. The facility operates under Hawaii state licensure and follows the Uniform Anatomical Gift Act (1968), which governs anatomical donation in the United States.

Primary users include orthopedic surgeons, neurosurgeons, plastic surgeons, dental specialists, and medical researchers from Japan and other countries. The center has supported research projects funded by Japan''s Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research (Kakenhi) and has exhibited at major Japanese medical society meetings, including the Japanese Orthopaedic Association, Japan Neurosurgical Society, and Japanese Society of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery. It also collaborates with Kauai Search & Rescue, providing cadavers for K-9 search dog training.

The center was founded to address the lack of accessible cadaver-based training environments in Japan, where legal restrictions limit anatomical dissection to specific university settings. By operating in Hawaii under U.S. law, it offers a legally compliant alternative for international medical professionals seeking realistic surgical practice and device validation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cadaver laboratory facility operation", "Surgical training and cadaveric workshop hosting", "Medical device testing and validation on cadaveric tissue", "Anatomical research support", "Cadaver procurement coordination with AATB-accredited tissue banks", "Continuing medical education program hosting", "K-9 search and rescue training support"], "industries": ["Medical education", "Surgical training", "Medical research", "Continuing medical education", "Orthopedic surgery", "Neurosurgery", "Plastic and reconstructive surgery", "Dental and oral surgery", "Medical device development", "Emergency services training"], "materials": ["Human cadaveric tissue (whole body and regional specimens)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Cadaver lab facility licensed by the State of Hawaii", "Donors screened and supplied by American Association of Tissue Banks", "Operates under Uniform Anatomical Gift Act (1968) legal framework", "Supports Japanese research grants (Kakenhi) with facility access", "Provides cadavers for K-9 search and rescue training programs"], "facts_used": ["Location: Honolulu, Hawaii -> db", "Purpose: Provide cadaver lab for medical education/research -> /", "Cadaver source: American Association of Tissue Banks -> /", "Legal basis: Uniform Anatomical Gift Act (1968) -> /", "Target users: Physicians, dentists, medical professionals -> /", "Research support: Japan Kakenhi grants -> /", "Conference exhibitions: Japanese Orthopaedic Association, Japan Neurosurgical Society, Japanese Society of Plasti