UPDATE companies SET description='I-Pull by Intermountain Auto operates a self-service automotive salvage yard at 3015 North 15th East in Idaho Falls, Idaho. The company describes itself as southeastern Idaho''s first self-service salvage yard, though a founding year is not publicly stated.

The yard allows customers to enter for a $2 per-person fee, bring their own hand or battery-powered tools, and remove parts directly from vehicles staged on site. Free equipment includes wheelbarrows, engine hoists, and manual tire-breakdown machines. I-Pull also purchases cars, trucks, vans, and SUVs in any condition, running or not. A daily-updated online inventory lets visitors search for specific vehicles before arriving. Pricing follows a published parts pricelist; core charges apply to certain components and can be refunded within 15 days with a receipt. General returns receive store credit within 30 days.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Self-service auto parts removal", "Vehicle purchasing (all makes/models, any condition)", "Online vehicle inventory search", "Published parts pricelist", "Core charge program", "30-day store credit return policy", "Free customer access to wheelbarrows, engine hoists, tire-breakdown machines"], "industries": ["Automotive repair", "Auto parts recycling", "Salvage yard operations"], "materials": ["Used automotive parts"], "equipment": ["Wheelbarrows", "Engine hoists", "Manual tire breakdown machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Southeastern Idaho''s first self-service salvage yard", "Customers bring their own tools and pull parts directly from vehicles", "Free use of wheelbarrows, engine hoists, and manual tire-breakdown machines", "Store credit returns within 30 days; core-charge refunds within 15 days", "Buys all makes and models, running or not"], "facts_used": ["Location: 3015 N 15th E, Idaho Falls, ID 83401 -> /", "Self-service salvage yard model -> /", "$2 per person entrance fee -> /", "Free customer equipment: wheelbarrows, engine hoists, manual tire breakdown machines -> /", "Buys all makes/models, running or not -> /", "Daily updated online inventory search -> /", "Published parts pricelist -> /", "Core charge refunds within 15 days with receipt -> /", "Store credit returns within 30 days with receipt -> /", "Hours: Mon-Fri 9AM-5PM, Sat 9AM-4PM, Closed Sundays -> /", "Yard rules: hand/battery tools only, no jacks/torches, 16+ entry, safety equipment recommended -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Southeastern Idaho''s first self-service salvage yard. Bring your own tools and pull your own parts.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='i-pull' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='I.C. Medical Inc. is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona. The company traces its origins to 1983, when Ioan and Elena Cosmescu emigrated from Romania and settled in Phoenix. Six years later, the couple launched I.C. Medical, establishing a business focused on surgical smoke evacuation. Ioan Cosmescu, a biomedical engineer and inventor, and Elena Cosmescu, a registered nurse and hospital administrator, brought deep healthcare experience to the venture.

Today, I.C. Medical develops and manufactures a range of surgical smoke evacuation devices, including the Crystal Vision® filtration system, the Telescopic PenEvac® and Non-Telescopic PenEvac® electrocautery pencils, as well as filters, sensors, and accessories. All products are produced, assembled, tested, and quality-assured in-house at the company’s 60,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Phoenix. The operation maintains total control over design, engineering, component sourcing, precision manufacturing, and packaging.

The company’s devices are used in surgical operating rooms worldwide, serving hospitals and surgical teams. I.C. Medical’s PenEvac® pencils are compatible with major smoke evacuator brands such as ConMed, Buffalo Filter, Stryker, Neptune, and Zimmer Biomet. The Crystal Vision® system is designed for open surgical procedures, while the PenEvac® line captures smoke at the source during electrosurgery.

I.C. Medical emphasizes its in-house production model as a differentiator, citing the risks of quality fade associated with outsourcing. The company holds 53 U.S. patents and more than 59 international patents for its smoke evacuation technologies. Its quality system is subject to regular audits by the FDA, ISO, CE, and CSA, and all products are made in the United States using virgin raw materials and proprietary processes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device design and development", "Precision manufacturing and assembly", "In-house testing and quality assurance", "Surgical smoke evacuation system manufacturing", "Electrocautery pencil manufacturing", "Filter and sensor manufacturing", "Regulatory compliance (FDA, ISO, CE, CSA)", "Proprietary process technology", "Virgin raw material sourcing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Surgical equipment", "Healthcare", "Operating room equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All devices manufactured in-house at a 60,000 sq ft facility in Phoenix, AZ", "Total control over design, engineering, component sourcing, and production", "Patented technology portfolio: 53 U.S. patents and 59+ international patents", "Products compatible with all major smoke evacuator brands (ConMed, Buffalo, Stryker, Neptune, Zimmer Biomet)", "Regular audits by FDA, ISO, CE, and CSA"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> /about", "Founders Ioan and Elena Cosmescu -> /about", "Company launched six years after 1983 emigration -> /about", "60,000 sq ft manufacturing facility in Phoenix -> /", "In-house manufacturing, assembly, testing, quality assurance -> /about", "Product lines: Crystal Vision system, PenEvac pencils, filters, sensors, accessories -> /about", "Compatibility with ConMed, Buffalo, Stryker, Neptune, Zimmer Biomet -> /", "53 U.S. patents and 59+ international patents held by Ioan Cosmescu -> /about", "Regular audits by FDA, ISO, CE, CSA -> /about", "Made in USA with virgin raw materials and proprietary processes -> /about", "Quality policy includes replacement warranty for defective products -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I.C. Medical manufactures the advanced Crystal Vision\u00ae surgical smoke evacuation and filtration system, the Telescopic PenEvac\u00ae electrocautery pencil, surgical smoke evacuation filters and sensors, and other surgical smoke evacuation system accessories.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='i-c-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='I.P.W. Auto Parts operates from a single location at 12040 W Feerick St in Wauwatosa, Wisconsin. The business traces its roots to Peter Tetzlaff, who began selling parts out of the back of his van; the operation has remained family-owned for roughly 40 years. Today the company is run by Sean and Mark Tetzlaff, with Kevin Stachowiak handling sales.

The store functions as a retail and wholesale outlet for automotive parts and supplies. Its inventory spans replacement parts, shop supplies, tires, oils and chemicals, and tools. Brand lines carried include Firestone, IronHead, Mastercraft, and Thunderer tires, along with a range of lubricants, cleaners, fillers, and primers. Customers can browse and purchase through an online catalog that supports vehicle-specific searches, as well as at the physical counter.

