UPDATE companies SET description='ICOMM Technologies Inc. was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Malvern, Pennsylvania. The fabless semiconductor company operates from an office Suite 210, and focuses on the design and development of wireless baseband processors for evolving mobile communication standards.

The company provides full custom ASIC design services and partners with back-end design house ICNexus and wafer foundry Fujitsu in Asia to deliver 90 nm and finer geometry ASIC design and fabrication. Its core expertise lies in 3G, 4G, and 5G baseband processor development, including beamforming, beamsteering, and array antenna technologies for 5G networks. ICOMM also conducts research into green energy technology for next-generation wireless systems.

ICOMM serves the wireless communications industry, supplying baseband processor solutions for smartphones, business automation, and autonomous vehicle applications. Its ASIC design and foundry services cater to semiconductor companies seeking low-cost, low-power, high-quality silicon with quick turnaround. The company''s green energy R&D targets sustainable technology for future mobile networks.

ICOMM differentiates itself through its fabless model combined with established Asian foundry partnerships, enabling deep submicron capabilities without owning fabrication facilities. The company emphasizes low-cost, low-power, high-quality ASIC services with rapid delivery, and positions itself as a leader in 5G baseband processor innovation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["ASIC design services", "ASIC foundry services (via partners)", "Back-end design services", "Wafer foundry services (via Fujitsu)", "5G baseband processor design", "Beamforming and beamsteering design", "Array antenna design", "Green energy technology R&D", "Wireless communication system design (3G/4G/5G)"], "industries": ["Wireless mobile communications", "5G infrastructure", "Semiconductor", "Green energy technology", "Automotive (autonomous vehicles)", "Industrial automation (business automation)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fabless model with Asian foundry partnerships for 90 nm and finer geometry ASIC production", "Full custom ASIC design services with low-cost, low-power, high-quality, quick-turn focus", "Expertise in 3G/4G/5G baseband processors, beamforming, beamsteering, and array antenna design", "Commitment to green energy technology R&D for next-generation wireless communications", "Self-described world leader in 3G/4G/5G baseband processor development"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> homepage", "Headquartered in Malvern, Pennsylvania -> homepage/db", "Fabless semiconductor company designing wireless baseband processors -> homepage", "Provides full custom ASIC design services -> homepage", "Partners with ICNexus (back-end design) and Fujitsu (wafer foundry) in Asia -> homepage", "Offers 90nm and finer geometry ASIC design and foundry services -> homepage", "Expertise in beamforming, beamsteering, array antenna for 5G -> homepage", "Committed to green energy technology R&D -> homepage", "Serves wireless communications, smartphone, business automation, autonomous car markets -> homepage", "YouTube channel: https://youtu.be/x6MWhlGZ2qU -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "IComm Technologies Inc., founded in 1998, is a fabless semiconductor company that designs, develops and markets high performance Wireless Baseband Processor for the new 3G/4G/5G Wireless Communication Systems.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://youtu.be/x6MWhlGZ2qU"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='icomm-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ID Medical Devices LLC operates from Fort Lauderdale, Florida, supplying medical devices and scientific equipment to healthcare and industrial buyers. The company''s website carries a 2023 copyright, though a founding year and ownership structure are not disclosed publicly. No founder names or background on the company''s origins appear in its public materials.

The firm distributes a catalog that includes the Stemtox-A, Eye Device, Elevare Red, Face & Body Slimming RF, and Full Body LED Device, alongside broader healthcare, industrial, and scientific supplies. It positions itself as a wholesale source, offering bulk purchasing and pricing described as lower than other suppliers. The company states that its up-to-date industrial knowledge enables it to cater to specialized procurement needs.

Customers span clinical practices, research facilities, and industrial operations that require medical-grade devices and related consumables. The company emphasizes direct communication for volume quotes and product inquiries, with a contact form that captures company name, contact details, and zip code to route requests.

