UPDATE companies SET description='Inanovate is based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. The company develops and manufactures Lyme-ID, an FDA 510(k)-cleared blood test for Lyme disease. No founding year or founder names are disclosed in public materials, and ownership structure has not been specified.

The Lyme-ID test uses Inanovate''s proprietary Bio-ID® technology with a single-step, modified two-tier methodology. Samples are collected at home using a pain-free upper arm device shipped in a kit that arrives within two days; the specimen is returned via prepaid packaging to the company''s CLIA-certified laboratory, where results are posted to a secure portal in as little as 24 hours. The test is priced at $200 per kit.

The company cites CDC data noting over 300,000 new U.S. cases annually and positions its test for early-stage sensitivity where standard methods often miss infections.

